From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:53:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime profile: every host site reads dm_profile(), the
 compiled macros are only its defaults

One host binary now runs another game's profile completely: main.c (module fallback, game_args), the save sync's title ID, core
preemption, display versions and the shared font, Unreal's texture pool, the operation and performance mode, StandardAllocator's
cap, the cheats' title and regions, the NVN API version, the texture upload switches, the shader key skip, frame pacing, the app
pool, conditional rendering, BC on the CPU, GPU timestamps, dynamic texture slots, vertex conversion, the pipeline archive switch,
present snapshots, the encode thread and the capture title. New profile keys: stdalloc_cap, shader_key_skip, tex_bc_cpu,
ue_texture_pool, enc_thread. game.py profile writes every key, with the none spellings where the game sets none, so a second
game's file never inherits the first game's compiled values. Hot paths read a cached pointer (dm_prof()). t_profile_runtime and
test_game_profile.py check it.

Upstream-Status: fork-only (completes 0001 runtime-profile, declined seedds/nxnative#492)
Reason: the route C shell runs several games on one host binary, so no host site may keep the compiled game's values. It builds on the runtime profile of 0001 and stays with it
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#144
